4 4. Or let dbplyr write the SQL


Code
tbl(con, "phenotypes") |&gt;
  left_join(tbl(con, "lines"), by = "line_id") |&gt;
  group_by(family, trait) |&gt;
  summarise(mean_val = mean(value), .groups = "drop") |&gt;
  show_query()


&lt;SQL&gt;
SELECT `family`, `trait`, AVG(`value`) AS `mean_val`
FROM (
  SELECT `phenotypes`.*, `name`, `family`
  FROM `phenotypes`
  LEFT JOIN `lines`
    ON (`phenotypes`.`line_id` = `lines`.`line_id`)
) AS `q01`
GROUP BY `family`, `trait`


Same dplyr verbs as Week 0b — translated to SQL and executed in the database.
